{
  "task_id": "lab-unit-harmonization",
  "top_k": 5,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_dd2c2bb21a85d21e3f37",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 7,
        "line_end": 7,
        "exact_text": "- incomplete records: some rows has missing values and could not be harmonized easily\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_ee057c2bf26f02ee8f80",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 8,
        "line_end": 8,
        "exact_text": "- scientific notation issue: you should convert `1.23e2` to something like `123.00`\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_667fa3e756df6d44ca40",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 9,
        "line_end": 9,
        "exact_text": "- decimal format: there are many ',' that should be interpreted as '.' (`12,34` is actually `12.34`). Also, there could be different decimal places randomly.\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_224549b42c039c94c473",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 10,
        "line_end": 11,
        "exact_text": "- the key issue -- mixed units: many values are using alternative units that might need your help to harmonize (e.g., µmol/L instead of mg/dL for creatinine, g/L instead of g/dL for hemoglobin)\r\n\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_95a146cd880ecd44215d",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 14,
        "line_end": 14,
        "exact_text": "1. remove patient rows with missing values as they cannot be recovered or harmonized\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_9ab28a129745f222ba0a",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 15,
        "line_end": 15,
        "exact_text": "2. handle scientific notation expression to the normal style\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_4e0ad0bac0394ac9cffd",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 16,
        "line_end": 16,
        "exact_text": "3. values outside the expected physiological ranges are more likely to be the ones using another unit. You need to switch the unit for them. Decide the range for physiological ranges for featrues, then apply the appropriate conversion factor to convert based on your knowledge and info.\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_4a40c0e0d4e99abac98c",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/lab-unit-harmonization/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 17,
        "line_end": 18,
        "exact_text": "4. round all values to 2 decimal places in such format: `X.XX`\r\n\r\n",
        "source_sha256": "e189c11747388583e83ff0e508fe315ea26be21c46e0a143dd5ec3ac24fb4c36",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
